WEBVTT

00:00.640 --> 00:07.280
The third element of your inner blueprint is your energy. And make no mistake, energy,

00:07.280 --> 00:14.560
not time, is your most valuable currency for high performance. You can't create more time in the day,

00:14.560 --> 00:19.440
but you absolutely can generate and protect more energy.

00:20.160 --> 00:26.080
Elite performers are masters of energy management. They are ruthless about identifying

00:26.080 --> 00:32.160
what fuels them and what drains them. I want you to think about your own work this week.

00:32.880 --> 00:37.440
What are your drains? Maybe it's that two-hour status meeting that could have been an email.

00:38.080 --> 00:42.960
Maybe it's navigating the internal politics. Be honest. Name them.

00:44.000 --> 00:50.240
Now, what are your fuels? Maybe it's that 30-minute one-on-one conversation where you get to mentor

00:50.240 --> 00:58.000
a junior colleague. Maybe it's that hour of deep, uninterrupted creative work. What activities make

00:58.000 --> 01:05.680
you lose track of the time in the best way? Understand your personal energy cycles is critical

01:05.680 --> 01:12.400
for sustainable success and is a core component of your wellbeing. The next activity in your

01:12.400 --> 01:19.600
playbook will guide you through a personal energy audit. You'll identify the people, the task,

01:19.600 --> 01:26.000
and the environments that either charge you up or deplete your reserves. This awareness

01:26.000 --> 01:36.960
is the first step towards redesigning your day and your work for peak performance.

